From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:40:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/videoout: the display gets a moment to settle at 119.88
 Hz before 59.94 Hz is restored

After VideoOut took the high-frame-rate mode, six vblank intervals were
measured at once and their median above 12.5 ms put 59.94 Hz back, for a
display that went on refreshing at 60 Hz (PS5_Vulkan, R31). Right after the
change the vblanks come irregularly while the display settles: a TV that
does refresh at 120 Hz measured 20.873 ms, and the Wii U side's frame
generation then stayed at 60 frames a second (PS5-ECAM issue 103).

The period is measured again until it is under the limit or 2.5 seconds
have gone by; only then is 59.94 Hz restored. The log says how long the
display took when it needed more than one measurement.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
index b6ef98a..f122d95 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
@@ -79,6 +79,10 @@
  * went on refreshing at 60 Hz, as a tester's did (PS5_Vulkan, R31). */
 #define VIDEOOUT_HIGH_REFRESH_LIMIT_NS UINT64_C(12500000)
 #define VIDEOOUT_PERIOD_INTERVALS 6
+/* How long the display gets to settle in the high-frame-rate mode before it is
+ * given up: right after the change its vblanks come irregularly, and a TV that
+ * does refresh at 120 Hz measured a median of 20.9 ms (PS5-ECAM issue 103). */
+#define VIDEOOUT_HIGH_REFRESH_SETTLE_NS UINT64_C(2500000000)
 /* param.json's attribute3 bit for 120 Hz output. PS5_Vulkan R31/R92 declared it with 0x80000
  * (a 120 Hz mode that requires VRR), which turns the system's VRR off; retail titles with VRR
  * declare 0x40 with 0x40000. VideoOut itself grants mode 15 or refuses it. */
@@ -387,13 +391,27 @@ videoout_configure_locked(struct wsi_videoout_output *out, bool high)
                     : supported;
    out->high_frame_rate = configured == 0;
    if (out->high_frame_rate) {
-      const uint64_t period = videoout_vblank_period_ns(out->handle);
+      /* Measured again while the display settles: 59.94 Hz only when the
+       * vblanks still come too slowly at the end of it. */
+      const uint64_t started = os_time_get_nano();
+      uint64_t period = videoout_vblank_period_ns(out->handle);
+      unsigned rounds = 1;
+      while (period > VIDEOOUT_HIGH_REFRESH_LIMIT_NS &&
+             os_time_get_nano() - started < VIDEOOUT_HIGH_REFRESH_SETTLE_NS) {
+         period = videoout_vblank_period_ns(out->handle);
+         rounds++;
+      }
+      const double waited_ms = (double)(os_time_get_nano() - started) / 1e6;
       if (period > VIDEOOUT_HIGH_REFRESH_LIMIT_NS) {
          sceVideoOutConfigureOutput(out->handle, PS5_VIDEO_OUT_MODE_RESTORE, NULL, NULL, NULL);
          out->high_frame_rate = false;
          fprintf(stderr,
-                 "wsi/videoout: 119.88 Hz accepted, but a vblank comes every %.3f ms; 59.94 Hz restored\n",
-                 (double)period / 1e6);
+                 "wsi/videoout: 119.88 Hz accepted, but a vblank comes every %.3f ms (after %.0f ms); "
+                 "59.94 Hz restored\n",
+                 (double)period / 1e6, waited_ms);
+      } else if (rounds > 1) {
+         fprintf(stderr, "wsi/videoout: 119.88 Hz, a vblank every %.3f ms once the display settled (%.0f ms)\n",
+                 (double)period / 1e6, waited_ms);
       }
    } else {
       fprintf(stderr, "wsi/videoout: 119.88 Hz %s (%d); presenting at 59.94 Hz\n",
